__pycache__/
*.pyc
.venv/
venv/
.env
.ipynb_checkpoints/
.pytest_cache/
*.egg-info/

# Claude Code's own tooling scratch space (e.g. isolated agent worktrees) —
# never part of the project.
.claude/

# Raw pulls are large and fully reproducible from the API/history archive —
# keep them out of git. Processed/projections/output ARE committed (plan §2,
# §8: the dashboard reads committed artefacts, never recomputes).
data/raw/

# v3 plan §E3: live Streamlit solve log — exploratory, per-user, local
# scratch. Never a canonical artefact; the pinned recommendation the log
# is graded against is data/output/gw{n}_recommendations.json, which IS
# committed.
data/scratch/

# Phase G (docs/superpowers/specs/2026-08-22-history-layer-design.md §3.7):
# the DuckDB read model and the derived manifest are both rebuildable from
# the immutable Parquet/JSON partitions under data/history/. Keeping the
# immutable thing immutable and the queryable thing disposable is the whole
# point — a bot-rewritten index committed on four crons a week would be a
# merge-conflict generator.
data/history/manifest.json
*.duckdb
